<task id="205g" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration — row A38b (customer.bicep secret-free gate on kvSecretValues (A38b — closes H2a re-seed vector))</title>
    <phase>Phase Pre-Live-Fire — Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration (task 205, A38b re-scope 2026-08-25)</phase>
    <gate>ready</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Per project CLAUDE.md rigor table + root §8.5 TEST-MODIFYING override: task tags include `auth` + `bicep` (Model 2 customer-stamp deployment template that drives the H2a InfraDeploy run — every future Model 2 customer's KV credential estate flows through this file); modifies `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` (BFF-adjacent — feeds `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` which is consumed by BFF runtime at boot); also updates + adds Bicep unit-style verification (`az bicep build` + `az deployment what-if` dry-run). Sibling A38a (task 205a) runs at Fable @ xhigh under FULL for the manifest half — A38b is the paired Bicep half that CLOSES THE H2A RE-SEED VECTOR that would otherwise nullify A38a (peer's verified evidence 2026-08-25: `customer.bicep:705/:713` writes both secrets on EVERY Model 2 H2a deploy, BEFORE H4 runs in the DAG — a manifest-only A38a reports "omitted" while the same run's H2a step already seeded both). Wrong gate = false-migrated trap = the exact silent-fail A38a exists to prevent; auth-tagged unconditional code-review + adr-check per root §8.5 TEST-MODIFYING override applies.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Per remediation plan §8 model-tier posture: "A38 + A42 on Fable/Opus … rest Sonnet-5 @ high". A38b is the Bicep-mechanics half of the re-scoped A38 (peer escalation 2026-08-25, owner approved) — deterministic Bicep conditional-object-property expression on a bounded surface (single map at `customer.bicep:704-715`; two keys gated; existing `signalrEnabled` bool param at `customer.bicep:78` is the exact template pattern; existing `SignalREnabled` RunParameter → deployment-param wiring at `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs:123 + :276-288` is the exact wiring template). No credential-selection reasoning (that lives in A38a's manifest branch on Fable). Sonnet-5 @ high is correct: literal execution of a template pattern with an explicit reference impl to copy; escalation triggers below handle the two known judgment boundaries (H2a wiring absent → add; ancillary bicep re-inject vector → stop).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Bicep-only under infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep + regenerated customer.json; disjoint from 205a A38a (KvSecretsPopulation/**), 205b A42 (EntraAppReg/**), 205h A38c (scripts/*.ps1), 205i A44.5 (EnvVarValues/**).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>A35 (landed); MUST land in same commit bundle as 205a A38a — A38a manifest omit alone re-opens the false-migrated trap if customer.bicep still re-seeds</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, auth, bicep, customer-stamp, secret-free-gate, kv-secret-values</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2h (per peer escalation re-scope 2026-08-25, owner approved)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Apply the re-scoped A38b half of punch row A38 (peer escalation 2026-08-25, owner approved) from `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` "A38 execution record" block. Gate `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep`'s `kvSecretValues` map (declared at `:704-715`) for `AiSearch--AdminKey` (`:705`) and `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` (`:713`) behind a NEW `requireSecretFreeIdentity` bool param (default `false`) using a Bicep conditional-object-property expression, so the downstream generated module `kv-secrets.generated.bicep`'s existing `if (contains(secretValues, ...))` skip-if-absent guard becomes EFFECTIVE on secret-free stamps. On `false` (default) behavior is bit-identical to today's `customer.bicep` (backwards compat preserved for pre-migration envs). On `true` the two keys are OMITTED from the map — never sentinel per auth-v4 §9.1 — so the module never writes them. Regenerate `infrastructure/bicep/customer.json` via `az bicep build`. Verify H2a → `customer.bicep` param wiring exists (RunParameter → deployment parameter) using the existing `signalrEnabled`/`SignalREnabledParameterKey` pattern at `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs:123 + :276-288` as reference — if the wiring does NOT exist, ADD it (do NOT skip A38b — the whole re-scope hinges on this gate). MUST NOT touch other `kvSecretValues` entries (Cosmos*, `Storage-ConnectionString`, `Redis-ConnectionString`, `DocumentIntelligence-*`, `AzureOpenAI-Endpoint`, `AppInsights-ConnectionString`, `Communication-WebhookUrl`, `AiSearch-Endpoint` — all UNCHANGED). MUST NOT touch `stacks/model1-shared.bicep` (Model 1 uses shared KV — different flow, out of scope for A38b). MUST land in the SAME COMMIT BUNDLE as 205a A38a — executor commits changes to the working tree via git add/status only; MAIN SESSION commits the bundle atomically after both siblings pass review. Amend punch-list annotations. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE Bicep/IaC author + L2 control-plane handler-Bicep-seam specialist. Expert in: `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` Model 2 customer-stamp template (structure: params → modules → `kvSecretValues` map → `kvSecrets` module invocation of `kv-secrets.generated.bicep`); Bicep conditional-object-property expression (the idiomatic `{ ...(cond ? { key: value } : {}) }` spread pattern for OMITTING keys); the existing `signalrEnabled` bool-param + module-if pattern at `customer.bicep:78 + :498` as the exact template shape; `az bicep build` regeneration of `customer.json` (must be checked in alongside the `.bicep` change — no drift); the H2a run-parameter → deployment-parameter wiring pattern in `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs` (const key at `:123`, `TryGetNonEmpty(...)` extraction at `:276`, mapped into the deploy request record at `:288`); the auth-v4 §9.1 sentinel ruling (OMIT-is-the-signal — never write a sentinel value into a credential slot; positive migration marker lives in a KV resource tag or `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field, applied by A38a's manifest branch, not by A38b); A23 clobber guard `contains(secretValues, ...)` skip-if-absent already present in `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` — A38b makes that guard EFFECTIVE by omitting the map key, NOT by removing/altering the guard itself.</role>

  <goal>
    - `customer.bicep` declares a NEW `param requireSecretFreeIdentity bool = false` (default `false` preserves current behavior for pre-migration envs — backwards compat).
    - On `requireSecretFreeIdentity == true`: the `kvSecretValues` map (currently `customer.bicep:704-715`) OMITS both `AiSearch--AdminKey` and `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` (Bicep conditional-object-property expression — the `{ ...(cond ? { key: value } : {}) }` spread pattern OR an equivalent verified-idiomatic construct).
    - Downstream: `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` receives a `secretValues` map WITHOUT the two keys when the flag is true → the existing `if (contains(secretValues, 'AiSearch--AdminKey'))` / `... 'ServiceBus-ConnectionString'` skip-if-absent guards fire as intended → the per-customer KV does NOT receive those two secrets on secret-free stamps.
    - `infrastructure/bicep/customer.json` regenerated via `az bicep build infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep`; no drift between `.bicep` source and `.json` ARM template (both are checked in together).
    - H2a handler (`H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs`) passes `requireSecretFreeIdentity` from run state (RunParameter, following the existing `signalrEnabled` pattern at `:123 + :276-288`) into the `customer.bicep` deployment param — either the wiring already exists (verify + document) or is ADDED in this task.
    - ALL OTHER `kvSecretValues` entries UNCHANGED — grep-confirm the following keys are still present with their current `FromBicepOutput` sources: `AiSearch-Endpoint`, `AppInsights-ConnectionString`, `AzureOpenAI-Endpoint`, `Communication-WebhookUrl`, `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey`, `DocumentIntelligence-Endpoint`, `Redis-ConnectionString`, `Storage-ConnectionString`.
    - Backwards compat preserved for pre-migration envs: default `false` means the map is bit-identical to today's; regenerated ARM template diff on default-false path is textually inert (only the new parameter declaration appears).
    - `az bicep build infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` succeeds (zero errors, zero new warnings vs pre-change baseline).
    - Dry-run verification: either `az bicep build` (compile only — minimum bar) OR `az deployment sub what-if` (preferred — proves param can be passed end-to-end against a test scope) succeeds.
    - `stacks/model1-shared.bicep` UNTOUCHED (grep-confirm zero diff vs pre-change).
    - Punch-list `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` "A38 execution record" block annotated with `last_known_status_after_execution` for A38b (paired with A38a's status).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>Peer escalation 2026-08-25 (task 205a, Fable @ xhigh, FULL rigor): the `partial-omit-set-discovered` escalation trigger fired at Step 2 grep-verify with zero code edits applied — because the LIVE upsert-site inventory for `AiSearch--AdminKey` + `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` extends beyond `StaticKvSecretManifest`. Site #1 in that inventory (the one that would nullify a manifest-only A38a): `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep:705` + `:713` UNCONDITIONALLY define `kvSecretValues` map entries for both keys (`AiSearch--AdminKey: aiSearch.outputs.searchServiceAdminKey` + `ServiceBus-ConnectionString: serviceBus.outputs.serviceBusConnectionString`). This feeds `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` whose `if (contains(secretValues, ...))` skip-if-absent guard ALWAYS fires under today's shape because both keys are always present in the map → both secrets are WRITTEN to the per-customer KV on EVERY Model 2 `customer.bicep` deploy (i.e. inside the provisioning DAG itself, at H2a — BEFORE H4 even runs). `customer.bicep:676-680`'s own comment confirms: this module call "is the actual value-writer H4 depends on". A manifest-only A38a would therefore report "omitted/migrated" in the H4 run record while the SAME RUN's H2a step had already seeded both secrets minutes earlier — the exact "falsely reports migrated" failure the escalation trigger names. Owner approved the A38 → A38a/A38b/A38c re-scope (+A44.5 for H7/task-142 half) 2026-08-25. A38b is the Bicep half: gate the map behind a bool param so the downstream skip-if-absent guard becomes effective. Reference template (verified in-tree 2026-08-25): the existing `signalrEnabled` bool at `customer.bicep:78` (default `false`) drives a module-if at `:498` — same shape as A38b's requirement. Reference wiring template (verified in-tree 2026-08-25): `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs:123` declares `SignalREnabledParameterKey = "signalrEnabled"`; `:276` extracts via `TryGetNonEmpty(parameters, SignalREnabledParameterKey, out var signalRaw)`; `:288` passes as `SignalREnabled: signalrEnabled` into the deploy request record. A38b's wiring MUST follow the same shape (either verify the existing shape covers `requireSecretFreeIdentity` or add a mirror pair `RequireSecretFreeIdentityParameterKey = "requireSecretFreeIdentity"` + `TryGetNonEmpty(...)` + record-field). Backwards compat is by construction: default `false` = today's behavior; only secret-free stamps flip the param via run parameters (which A38a's H4 handler already reads via the FR-39 `ficOmitSecretNames`/`OmitCanonicalNames` seam per task 126 — verify wiring parity or document divergence).</background>
