  <constraints>
    <constraint source="peer escalation 2026-08-25, owner approved re-scope">A38b's landing spot is `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` ONLY (plus regenerated `customer.json` and, if wiring missing, `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs`). Executor MUST NOT expand scope to `Rotate-Secrets.ps1` / `Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1` / `Provision-Customer.ps1` — those belong to A38c (task 205h). MUST NOT expand into `StaticKvSecretManifest.cs` / `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` — those belong to A38a (task 205a). MUST NOT expand into H7/H6 `EnvVarValues__ClientSecret` — that belongs to A44.5 (task 205i).</constraint>
    <constraint source="peer inventory 2026-08-25">`kv-secrets.generated.bicep` skip-if-absent (`if (contains(secretValues, ...))`) guards are ALREADY CORRECT — the fix is in the CALLER (`customer.bicep` map), not in the generated module. MUST NOT modify `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` (it is generated; also A23 clobber guard lives there and must not regress). Executor VERIFIES the guards are present + effective post-change; does not touch them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 + azure-deployment.md">Regenerate `infrastructure/bicep/customer.json` via `az bicep build infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` after every `.bicep` edit; commit `.bicep` and `.json` together (no drift). Verify with `git diff --stat` that both files change together on the default-false path (only the new param declaration appears; ARM template functional behavior unchanged on default).</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 §9.1 sentinel ruling (via A35)">A38b OMITS the two keys from the map when `requireSecretFreeIdentity == true`. MUST NOT substitute a sentinel value (empty string, `null`-as-string, placeholder GUID, etc.) — sentinel resolution produces opaque `AADSTS7000215` at BFF runtime, indistinguishable from a real misconfiguration in operator triage. The positive migration marker (KV resource tag / `sprk_dataverseenvironment` state field) is A38a's responsibility, not A38b's.</constraint>
    <constraint source="peer verified reference template 2026-08-25">The existing `signalrEnabled` bool at `customer.bicep:78` + its H2a wiring at `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs:123 + :276 + :288` IS the template to follow. Deviations from this pattern (different naming convention, different extraction helper, param declared in a different section) MUST be justified in task notes — Sonnet-5 literal-execution posture is "copy this pattern".</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope-fence verified 2026-08-25">MUST NOT touch other `kvSecretValues` entries. Only `AiSearch--AdminKey` (`:705`) and `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` (`:713`) are gated. Grep-confirm post-change that `Cosmos*`, `Storage-ConnectionString`, `Redis-ConnectionString`, `DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey`, `DocumentIntelligence-Endpoint`, `AzureOpenAI-Endpoint`, `AppInsights-ConnectionString`, `Communication-WebhookUrl`, `AiSearch-Endpoint` are still present in the map with their existing `FromBicepOutput`-source expressions unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope-fence — Model 1 out of scope">MUST NOT touch `infrastructure/bicep/stacks/model1-shared.bicep`. Model 1 uses a shared KV via a different flow; A38b is Model 2 customer-stamp only. Grep-confirm zero diff in `stacks/model1-shared.bicep` post-change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="backwards compat — pre-migration envs">Default `requireSecretFreeIdentity = false` preserves today's behavior EXACTLY for every pre-migration Model 2 stamp. Any existing deployment re-run WITHOUT flipping the param must produce a bit-identical `kvSecretValues` map (verified via `az bicep build` diff on the ARM output — new parameter declaration is the only expected addition).</constraint>
    <constraint source="BINDING sequencing with A38a (task 205a)">A38b MUST land in the SAME COMMIT BUNDLE as A38a. Rationale: A38a alone re-opens the false-migrated trap (H2a re-seeds); A38b alone omits the map keys but A38a's positive migration marker is what tells operators the env is secret-free. Executor does NOT commit — after implementation completes, executor runs `git status` + `git diff --stat` for both A38b's files and reports readiness to main session; main session commits the bundle atomically only after A38a + A38b both pass review.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">All edits in this task are OUTSIDE `.claude/**` (only `infrastructure/**` and `src/server/**`), so a sub-agent may perform them. If A38b needs to update the punch-list annotation in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` (project-scoped `notes/`, not `.claude/`), executor may edit directly. Do NOT touch `.claude/skills/**` or `.claude/constraints/**` in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 component justification">A38b EXTENDS an existing file (`customer.bicep`) — no NEW component created. If wiring must be added in `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs`, that too EXTENDS an existing handler following the exact `signalrEnabled` precedent (no new abstraction, no new interface). Reflected in §11 justification (notes section).</constraint>
    <constraint source="A23 no-regress">`kv-secrets.generated.bicep`'s `contains(secretValues, ...)` skip-if-absent + `never-declared` guards remain intact. Post-change grep MUST confirm both terms still present (`skip-if-absent` behavior + `never-declared` array). If either regresses, STOP.</constraint>
  </constraints>

