  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, high effort, sonnet). Read this POML in full. Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` lines 76-107 (A38 execution record + proposed re-scope + A38b row). Read `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` §"Owner refinements 2026-08-25" for §6.5 context. Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-remediation-plan.md` §5 (silent-failure catalog) + §7 (sequencing) + §8 (effort) for cross-reference. Read project CLAUDE.md MUST rules block. Read `.claude/constraints/auth.md` + `.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md` + `.claude/constraints/provisioning.md`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep-verify current state (BEFORE any edit)">Run these greps + record findings in scratchpad table BEFORE touching any file: (a) `grep -n "kvSecretValues" infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` — expect the map at `:704-715` (confirm line numbers; if refactored since 2026-08-25, RECONCILE with latest before editing per Escalation trigger 1). (b) `grep -n "AiSearch--AdminKey\|ServiceBus-ConnectionString" infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` — expect `:705` + `:713`. (c) `grep -n "signalrEnabled" infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` — capture the exact param-declaration shape at `:78` (this is the template). (d) `grep -n "SignalREnabled\|signalrEnabled" src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BicepInfraDeploy/H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs` — expect const at `:123`, extraction at `:276`, record-field at `:288`. (e) `grep -n "contains(secretValues" scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/generated/kv-secrets.generated.bicep` — confirm skip-if-absent guards present (A23 no-regress baseline). (f) `grep -n "requireSecretFreeIdentity" infrastructure/ src/server/` — expect ZERO matches (proves this is a NEW param, not a duplicate).</step>
    <step order="2" name="Verify (or plan to add) H2a wiring">Read `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs:107-140` (parameter-key const block) + `:220-295` (parameter-extraction + deploy-request assembly). Determine: does H2a already pass an arbitrary run-parameter to `customer.bicep` deployment param `requireSecretFreeIdentity`? If YES (verify by walking the code path), document it. If NO, PLAN the wiring: add `RequireSecretFreeIdentityParameterKey = "requireSecretFreeIdentity"` const at ~`:124`, add `TryGetNonEmpty(...)` extraction at ~`:277`, add `RequireSecretFreeIdentity: requireSecretFreeIdentity` field to the deploy request record at ~`:288-289`. Verify the deploy-request record type accepts the new field (may require updating the record definition — trace the type). If the wiring requires substantial refactor beyond the trivial mirror-add pattern, STOP + escalate per Escalation trigger 2.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Checkpoint (after load + grep + wiring analysis)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="4" name="Edit customer.bicep — add param">Add `param requireSecretFreeIdentity bool = false` near the existing `signalrEnabled` param at `customer.bicep:78`. Add a `@description(...)` decorator explaining the param: "When true, OMIT `AiSearch--AdminKey` and `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` from the per-customer KV kvSecretValues map (auth-v4 §9.1 sentinel-free contract; A38b re-scope 2026-08-25; the downstream `kv-secrets.generated.bicep` skip-if-absent guard fires when the key is absent). Default false preserves current behavior for pre-migration envs."</step>
    <step order="5" name="Edit customer.bicep — gate the two map entries">Replace the two unconditional entries at `:705` + `:713` with a conditional-object-property expression. Preferred pattern (idiomatic Bicep — verify against `az bicep build` output): a spread-conditional `union()` construct OR the `{ ...(cond ? { key: value } : {}) }` spread form, whichever compiles cleanly. Concretely, restructure the `kvSecretValues` declaration so that when `requireSecretFreeIdentity == false` the map is bit-identical to today's (all 10 keys present), and when `true` exactly two keys (`AiSearch--AdminKey` + `ServiceBus-ConnectionString`) are omitted while all 8 other keys remain. Preserve the header comment block at `:680-702` (documents which entries are Resolvable vs Deliberately OMITTED — extend it briefly to note the new secret-free-gate semantics for the two keys).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Regenerate customer.json">Run `az bicep build infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep`. Verify zero errors, zero new warnings vs pre-change baseline. Verify `customer.json` file mtime updated. Run `git diff --stat infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep infrastructure/bicep/customer.json` — both files must appear.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Add H2a wiring (if planned in Step 2)">IF Step 2 determined wiring must be added: EDIT `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs` following the exact `signalrEnabled` pattern (const at parameter-key block, `TryGetNonEmpty(...)` extraction, deploy-request field). Update the deploy-request record type if needed. Update the small `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandlerTests.cs` if it asserts on the parameter set (mirror the `signalrEnabled` test case). If Step 2 determined wiring already exists, SKIP this step + document.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Checkpoint (after 3 code steps)">Run `context-handoff`.</step>
