  <notes>Justification (root CLAUDE.md §11): **Existing** — `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` is the sole Model 2 customer-stamp template (per project CLAUDE.md MUST rule "customer.bicep is the sole Model2Dedicated template"); the `kvSecretValues` map at `:704-715` is the exact site H2a's re-seed vector flows through (peer's verified evidence 2026-08-25). **Extension** — A38b EXTENDS `customer.bicep` with a NEW bool param `requireSecretFreeIdentity` (default `false` — backwards compat by construction) following the exact existing `signalrEnabled` template pattern at `:78`. NO NEW abstraction, NO NEW module, NO NEW interface; the wiring in H2a (if added) mirrors the exact existing `SignalREnabledParameterKey` const + `TryGetNonEmpty(...)` + deploy-request-field triple at `H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.cs:123 + :276 + :288`. **Cost-of-doing-nothing** — concrete failure mode: without A38b, `customer.bicep`'s H2a step unconditionally writes `AiSearch--AdminKey` + `ServiceBus-ConnectionString` to the per-customer KV on EVERY Model 2 deploy (before H4 runs in the DAG). A38a's manifest omit filter would then report "omitted/migrated" in the H4 run record while the SAME RUN's H2a step had already seeded both secrets minutes earlier — the exact false-migrated trap the peer's escalation names. Under `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true` at BFF boot, the freshly re-seeded secret sits BENEATH MI-FIC and either (a) fail-fasts the boot with an opaque error (peer's "boot loops fresh stamp" mode per remediation plan §8), or (b) silently absorbs a broken FIC with green health signals — the strictly-worse-than-no-migration failure mode auth-v4's `auth.md` documents. A38b is the paired Bicep half that CLOSES this vector; A38a alone is a false migration. **BLOCKS-186 in bundle with A38a** per punch-row A38's blocks-186 flag and the peer's re-scope disposition. Wiring parity with A38a's H4 handler (which reads run-parameter `ficOmitSecretNames` / `OmitCanonicalNames` per task 126) verified in Step 2 or documented divergence + rationale.</notes>

